Subject: [PATCH 0014] sh4: advance MMUCR.URC on UTLB misses, not on every fill

# melco-nav-emu core patch.
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
# Copyright (c) 2026 melco-nav-emu contributors
# Modifies GPL-licensed QEMU sources; applied by scripts/qemu.sh.

find_utlb_entry() runs once per softmmu TLB fill and advanced URC each
time.  How often QEMU refills a page it has already translated (TLB
resizes, code-TLB lookups after the execution loop exits) depends on host
timing, and the guest's LDTLB writes the UTLB entry URC selects, so the
guest's own TLB contents and TLB-miss exceptions differed between two
-icount shift=3,sleep=off boots of the same CU-P2006 image.

URC now advances when the UTLB lookup misses, i.e. once per TLB-miss
exception the guest sees, so a miss handler's LDTLB fills the UTLB round
robin.  The memory-mapped UTLB array accesses keep their per-access
increment.  Real hardware advances URC on every UTLB access; neither the
old nor the new count is cycle-accurate, but this one follows guest events
only.

--- a/target/sh4/helper.c
+++ b/target/sh4/helper.c
@@ -316,11 +316,22 @@
    Return entry, MMU_DTLB_MISS, MMU_DTLB_MULTIPLE */
 static int find_utlb_entry(CPUSH4State *env, vaddr address, int use_asid)
 {
-    /* per utlb access */
-    increment_urc(env);
+    int e = find_tlb_entry(env, address, env->utlb, UTLB_SIZE, use_asid);
 
-    /* Return entry */
-    return find_tlb_entry(env, address, env->utlb, UTLB_SIZE, use_asid);
+    /*
+     * The hardware advances URC on every UTLB access.  This function runs
+     * once per softmmu TLB fill, and how often QEMU refills a page it has
+     * already translated depends on its TLB sizing and on where the
+     * execution loop exits, which follow host timing.  Since LDTLB writes
+     * the entry URC selects, counting those refills made the guest's TLB
+     * contents differ between identical icount runs.  Advance URC only
+     * when the lookup misses, i.e. once per TLB-miss exception the guest
+     * sees (melco-nav-emu).
+     */
+    if (e == MMU_DTLB_MISS) {
+        increment_urc(env);
+    }
+    return e;
 }
 
